# Desecration Demon: the sacrifice is a choice and may be declined (CR 701.21a): on turn 2 Bot2 declines, so the Demon stays a 6/6 and Bot2 keeps its Memnite. On turn 3, at the beginning of
# Bot1's own combat, Bot2 sacrifices the Memnite: the Demon becomes a tapped 7/7 before attackers are declared, so Bot2 takes no damage from it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Desecration Demon
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Desecration Demon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Choose
? Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Power = 6
? Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Memnite)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Power = 7
Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Tapped = true
